<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH SHELL RAISES GASOLINE, DIESEL PRICES.</title>
<headline>DUTCH SHELL RAISES GASOLINE, DIESEL PRICES.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell unit Shell Nederland BV said on Thursday it would raise its pump prices of gasoline in the Netherlands by one cent per litre and of diesel by 1.2 cents per litre effective from December 7.</p>
<p>The move reflects changes in international product prices and the value of the dollar against the guilder, the firm said.</p>
<p>From Thursday the price of premium unleaded gasoline at Shell pumps will rise to 2.08 guilders per litre. The price of premium with lead substitute will rise to 2.14 guilders/litre and that of Euro regular unleaded to 2.03 guilders.</p>
<p>The recommended price for diesel will rise to 1.514 guilders per litre, Shell said.</p>
